<edge source="iran_gulf_conflict::military_escalation_leve" target="israel_palestine_conflic::ceasefire_stability" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.75</data>
  <data key="d37">Heightened military escalation in the Gulf raises perceived risk of wider regional war and incentivizes militant actors (e.g., Hamas, Hezbollah) and state patrons to test or abandon temporary truces, reducing the perceived durability of ceasefires.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">iran_gulf_conflict</data>
  <data key="d40">israel_palestine_conflic</data>
</edge>
<edge source="iran_gulf_conflict::military_escalation_leve" target="israel_palestine_conflic::diplomatic_mediation" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.7</data>
  <data key="d37">Rising Gulf military tensions trigger third-party states (US, Qatar, Egypt, EU) to intensify shuttle diplomacy and mediation in Israel–Palestine to prevent spillover and manage parallel crisis channels.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">iran_gulf_conflict</data>
  <data key="d40">israel_palestine_conflic</data>
</edge>
<edge source="iran_gulf_conflict::military_escalation_leve" target="russia_ukraine_war::military_support_stock" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.75</data>
  <data key="d37">A sharp escalation in the Gulf prompts the US and European suppliers to reprioritize and redirect finite stocks of air-defense munitions, interceptors and urgent battlefield supplies to partners in the Middle East, delaying or reducing shipments earmarked for Ukraine.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">iran_gulf_conflict</data>
  <data key="d40">russia_ukraine_war</data>
</edge>
<edge source="iran_gulf_conflict::military_escalation_leve" target="russia_ukraine_war::air_defense_capacity" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.7</data>
  <data key="d37">Heightened Gulf conflict leads states to forward-deploy or transfer SAM systems and spares to regional partners and consume reserve interceptors, directly reducing the pool of operational air-defence assets available for transfer to Ukrainian forces.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">iran_gulf_conflict</data>
  <data key="d40">russia_ukraine_war</data>
</edge>
