<edge source="iran_gulf_conflict::attacks_on_shipping_rate" target="israel_palestine_conflic::cross_border_strikes" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.65</data>
  <data key="d37">A surge in attacks on commercial shipping attributed to Iran or its proxies prompts Israeli kinetic reprisals and pre-emptive strikes against Iran-aligned groups in Lebanon/Syria, increasing the frequency and intensity of cross‑border strikes.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">iran_gulf_conflict</data>
  <data key="d40">israel_palestine_conflic</data>
</edge>
<edge source="iran_gulf_conflict::attacks_on_shipping_rate" target="israel_palestine_conflic::security_incident_rate" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">1</data>
  <data key="d36">0.55</data>
  <data key="d37">Increased attacks on shipping raise regional alert levels and produce short-term operational upticks (raids, interdictions, clashes) by state and non‑state actors across neighboring fronts, raising the rate of discrete security incidents.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">iran_gulf_conflict</data>
  <data key="d40">israel_palestine_conflic</data>
</edge>
<edge source="iran_gulf_conflict::attacks_on_shipping_rate" target="russia_ukraine_war::drone_diffusion_rate" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.6</data>
  <data key="d37">Increased attacks on commercial shipping accelerate operational learning and create demand for maritime loitering and kamikaze drone designs, which are then copied, brokered or exported and adapted into other theaters including the Russia–Ukraine conflict.</data>
  <data key="d38">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d39">iran_gulf_conflict</data>
  <data key="d40">russia_ukraine_war</data>
</edge>
<edge source="iran_gulf_conflict::attacks_on_shipping_rate" target="us_asia_alliance_stress::diplomacy_engagement_rat" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.8</data>
  <data key="d37">An increase in attacks on commercial shipping forces more frequent formal and informal diplomatic contacts (coalition meetings, port-state consultations, flag-state coordination) to organize escorts, information-sharing, and legal responses.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">iran_gulf_conflict</data>
  <data key="d40">us_asia_alliance_stress</data>
</edge>
<edge source="iran_gulf_conflict::attacks_on_shipping_rate" target="us_asia_alliance_stress::deterrence_credibility" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.6</data>
  <data key="d37">If attacks on shipping continue despite allied presence and defensive measures, partners perceive defenses as ineffective and adversaries as willing to accept costs, reducing perceived deterrence credibility.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">iran_gulf_conflict</data>
  <data key="d40">us_asia_alliance_stress</data>
</edge>
<edge source="iran_gulf_conflict::attacks_on_shipping_rate" target="us_china_rivalry::compute_infrastructure_c" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.7</data>
  <data key="d37">A spike in attacks on commercial shipping delays and diverts shipments of GPUs, networking and server hardware, forcing postponement of planned data-center builds and short-term reductions in available compute infrastructure capacity.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">iran_gulf_conflict</data>
  <data key="d40">us_china_rivalry</data>
</edge>
