</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::drone_diffusion_rate" target="iran_gulf_conflict::attacks_on_shipping_rate" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.75</data>
  <data key="d37">Maritime-capable drones, sensors and tactical lessons diffused from the Ukraine conflict are adopted by Gulf state and proxy actors, enabling more frequent remote strikes and harassing attacks on commercial vessels.</data>
  <data key="d38">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d40">iran_gulf_conflict</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::drone_diffusion_rate" target="israel_palestine_conflic::cross_border_strikes" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.8</data>
  <data key="d37">Rapid operational diffusion of attack drones and counter-drone tactics from the Ukraine theatre to regional actors and illicit suppliers increases non-state and proxy capability to conduct long-range, cross-boundary strike missions against adversary territory.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d40">israel_palestine_conflic</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::drone_diffusion_rate" target="us_asia_alliance_stress::joint_drill_intensity" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.7</data>
  <data key="d37">As UAS capabilities and tactics proven in Ukraine spread to other state and non-state actors, U.S. and Asian allies increase the frequency and scope of joint counter-UAS, ISR and layered-defense exercises to develop tactics, sensors, and rules of engagement.</data>
  <data key="d38">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d40">us_asia_alliance_stress</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::drone_diffusion_rate" target="us_china_rivalry::compute_infrastructure_c" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.6</data>
  <data key="d37">Faster diffusion of autonomous and swarm drone tactics raises near-term demand for training, simulation and edge/cloud compute for both offensive autonomy and defensive counter-AI systems, prompting accelerated deployment and procurement of compute infrastructure by governments and firms involved in the US–China competition.</data>
  <data key="d38">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d40">us_china_rivalry</data>
</edge>
