<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::military_support_stock" target="iran_gulf_conflict::military_escalation_leve" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.6</data>
  <data key="d37">Large volumes of external military support directed to the Ukraine theater draw Western naval/air assets and political bandwidth away from the Gulf, lowering short-term deterrence and prompting regional actors to increase coercive operations and demonstrations of force.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d40">iran_gulf_conflict</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::military_support_stock" target="israel_palestine_conflic::diplomatic_mediation" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.65</data>
  <data key="d37">A surge in external military support directed toward Ukraine diverts political attention, logistical resources, and diplomatic capital of key mediators (notably Western governments), reducing the intensity and persistence of third‑party mediation efforts in the Israel–Palestine system.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d40">israel_palestine_conflic</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::military_support_stock" target="us_asia_alliance_stress::alliance_policy_alignmen" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.6</data>
  <data key="d37">Sustained drawdowns and diversion of Western military stocks to support Ukraine create immediate supply and prioritization pressures that produce differing burden-sharing responses and timetables among Asian partners, eroding short-term policy alignment within the alliance.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d40">us_asia_alliance_stress</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::military_support_stock" target="us_china_rivalry::ai_hardware_capex_rate" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.7</data>
  <data key="d37">An increase in international military support that includes or highlights reliance on advanced Western chips and AI-enabled systems prompts tighter export controls/tech denial and causes Chinese state and industry to accelerate domestic AI hardware capital expenditures to substitute for restricted imports.</data>
  <data key="d38">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d40">us_china_rivalry</data>
</edge>
