<edge source="us_china_rivalry::ai_capital_inflow_rate" target="iran_gulf_conflict::market_price_volatility" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.6</data>
  <data key="d37">Large, rapid inflows into AI-focused trading firms and quant funds expand the share of AI-driven algorithmic trading in crude and product markets, increasing short-term liquidity swings and realized/implied price volatility.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">us_china_rivalry</data>
  <data key="d40">iran_gulf_conflict</data>
</edge>
<edge source="us_china_rivalry::ai_capital_inflow_rate" target="russia_ukraine_war::military_support_stock" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.6</data>
  <data key="d37">Rising private and public investment into dual-use AI firms increases production, inventories and rapid commercial-to-government procurement of ISR, autonomous loitering munitions and related systems that can be purchased or donated to parties in the conflict.</data>
  <data key="d38">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d39">us_china_rivalry</data>
  <data key="d40">russia_ukraine_war</data>
</edge>
<edge source="us_china_rivalry::ai_capital_inflow_rate" target="us_asia_alliance_stress::joint_drill_intensity" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.7</data>
  <data key="d37">A rapid rise in AI-directed capital flows into defense contractors and integrators accelerates procurement and fielding schedules for AI-enabled systems, creating immediate interoperability and command-and-control integration needs that allies meet by increasing the scale and frequency of joint exercises.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">us_china_rivalry</data>
  <data key="d40">us_asia_alliance_stress</data>
</edge>
