<edge source="us_china_rivalry::ai_hardware_capex_rate" target="israel_palestine_conflic::cross_border_strikes" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.7</data>
  <data key="d37">Higher AI-focused hardware capex expands global production and supply of advanced chips, sensors and combat drones that regional states and proxies can procure or indigenize, increasing the frequency and precision of strikes that cross borders.</data>
  <data key="d38">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d39">us_china_rivalry</data>
  <data key="d40">israel_palestine_conflic</data>
</edge>
<edge source="us_china_rivalry::ai_hardware_capex_rate" target="russia_ukraine_war::drone_diffusion_rate" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.7</data>
  <data key="d37">Higher capex for AI hardware expands production capacity for AI-specific chips and edge compute modules, lowering unit costs and increasing availability of high-performance autopilot and vision stacks that flow into commercial and gray-market drone manufacturers used in the Russia-Ukraine theater.</data>
  <data key="d38">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d39">us_china_rivalry</data>
  <data key="d40">russia_ukraine_war</data>
</edge>
<edge source="us_china_rivalry::ai_hardware_capex_rate" target="us_asia_alliance_stress::diplomacy_engagement_rat" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.6</data>
  <data key="d37">A visible surge in adversary AI hardware capital spending (chips, datacenters, sensors) prompts regional partners and the U.S. to initiate intensified diplomatic consultations and outreach to coordinate responses, intelligence sharing, and reassurance measures.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">us_china_rivalry</data>
  <data key="d40">us_asia_alliance_stress</data>
</edge>
